 ## Overview
-Manifold Next Event Estimation (MNEE) Improvement is an optimization for volumetric path tracing that estimates direct lighting by searching for a point within the participating medium that satisfies Fermat’s principle, rather than walking along surface boundaries. It addresses the limitations of standard NEE and original MNEE in scenes with refractive boundaries and complex geometry, specifically targeting highly directional, near-delta light distributions. It builds on [Next Event Estimation for Volumetric Path Tracing](1125-next-event-estimation-for-volumetric-path-tracing.md) by refining the connection strategy for media surrounded by refractive boundaries.
